<title>PERU: Peru says February sugar cane output off 0.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Peru says February sugar cane output off 0.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-04-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's sugar cane production fell 0.6 percent in February to 511,490 tonnes, compared with the same month last year, the Agriculture Ministry said Monday.</p>
<p>Sugar cane production for the first two months of the year dipped to 1.037 million tonnes from 1.066 million tonnes in the same period last year, the ministry said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>Total sugar imports fell 28.4 percent in February to $4.9 million compared to the same month last year, while imports in the first two months dropped 18.9 percent to $13.2 million, compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>According to the ministry's latest figures, sugar cane exports in January were up 36.6 percent to $10.32 million, compared to the same month in 1995.</p>
<p>((-- Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134))</p>
